uld, shouldn't, have to or don't have to?","prompt":"The museum is free — you ___ pay.","options":["shouldn't","don't have to","don't should"],"answer":"don't have to"},{"stage":"Practice","type":"choice","title":"Part 1 — should, shouldn't, have to or don't have to?","prompt":"You ___ drink the tap water there. (bad idea)","options":["don't have to","don't should","shouldn't"],"answer":"shouldn't"},{"stage":"Practice","type":"choice","title":"take, miss, go — the transport verbs. Listen, then choose.","prompt":"You ___ the train or the bus.","options":["take","miss","missed"],"answer":"take"},{"stage":"Practice","type":"choice","title":"take, miss, go — the transport verbs. Listen, then choose.","prompt":"You were late and the bus left. You ___ the bus.","options":["took","take","missed"],"answer":"missed"},{"stage":"Practice","type":"choice","title":"take, miss, go — the transport verbs. Listen, then choose.","prompt":"No transport — you go ___ foot.","options":["by","on","take"],"answer":"on"},{"stage":"Practice","type":"choice","title":"take, miss, go — the transport verbs. Listen, then choose.","prompt":"You go ___ bike or ___ car.","options":["on / on","by / by","silent — not pronounced"],"answer":"by / by"},{"stage":"Listening","type":"rows","title":"Advice from someone who lived in Moscow for three years.","sub":"","track":"A1_L28_8_9.mp3","items":[{"q":"How long did she live in Moscow?","options":["Two months","Ten years","Three years"],"answer":"Three years"},{"q":"The Underground was built…","options":["last year","in the 1930s","in the 1990s"],"answer":"in the 1930s"},{"q":"What does she say about the buses?","options":["They are empty.","They are usually full.","There are no buses."],"answer":"They are usually full."}]}]}